      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the review and insights! Your comments on processOne and renames prompted a bit of a redesign, and the new patchset is hopefully simpler and a bit more robust.\n\nInstead of jumping over commits in the commit graph (which missed renames and assumed line offsets didn\u0027t change), we now let ignored commits flow through standard processOne / processMerge diff processing.\n\n1. Normal blame diffs child vs parent, and attributes modified lines to the child.\n2. When the child commit is in ignoreIds, Candidate.takeBlame() translates those modified line coordinates into the parent\u0027s coordinate space (Candidate.addIgnoredEdit) and transfers them to the parent candidate instead of claiming them on the child.\n3. File renames, line additions/deletions, and multi-parent merges now work naturally out of the box using JGit\u0027s existing diff pipeline.\n\nThe custom graph-bypassing logic (getEffectiveParents, findNonIgnoredAncestors, cloneRegionList) and the bypass block in next() have been completely removed.",
      "parentUuid": "7f0e52f5_dc071ac9",
      "revId": "314d29b3e97dc98b87a3668d41a1175660db989d",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
